net80211: publish each radio as an IO80211Controller registry entry

A net80211 radio (struct ieee80211com, "iwlwifi0") is neither a newbus
device of its own nor an ifnet, so nothing in NextBSD's IORegistry marks
the moment it becomes usable. iwlwifi, for one, loads its firmware
asynchronously and calls ieee80211_ifattach() seconds after its newbus
node attached. wland, which clones the VAP and runs wpa_supplicant,
could only poll net.wlan.devices for it, and never noticed a radio go.

Publish a virtual IORegistry entry of class IO80211Controller, named
after the radio, at the end of ieee80211_ifattach(), once the radio is
on the list net.wlan.devices reads, and retire it at the end of
ieee80211_ifdetach(), once its VAPs are destroyed and it is off that
list. wland matches it with IOServiceAddMatchingNotification
(first-match and terminated), as Darwin's wifid follows
IO80211Controller. The entry itself is built in ieee80211_ioreg.c (this
directory's src/), with the kernel's ioreg_publish_virtual() and
ioreg_retire_virtual(), as iokit_hid.c does for IOHIDDevice.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-userland#502). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/net80211/ieee80211.c

--- a/sys/net80211/ieee80211.c
+++ b/sys/net80211/ieee80211.c
@@ -58,6 +58,9 @@
 
 #include <net/bpf.h>
 
+/* NextBSD: IO80211Controller registry entries (nextbsd-userland#502). */
+#include "ieee80211_ioreg.h"
+
 const char *ieee80211_phymode_name[IEEE80211_MODE_MAX] = {
 	[IEEE80211_MODE_AUTO]	  = "auto",
 	[IEEE80211_MODE_11A]	  = "11a",
@@ -359,6 +362,12 @@
 	mtx_lock(&ic_list_mtx);
 	LIST_INSERT_HEAD(&ic_head, ic, ic_next);
 	mtx_unlock(&ic_list_mtx);
+
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: publish the radio as an IO80211Controller registry entry,
+	 * now that net.wlan.devices lists it (nextbsd-userland#502).
+	 */
+	ieee80211_ioreg_publish(ic);
 }
 
 /*
@@ -418,6 +427,12 @@
 	taskqueue_free(ic->ic_tq);
 	IEEE80211_TX_LOCK_DESTROY(ic);
 	IEEE80211_LOCK_DESTROY(ic);
+
+	/*
+	 * NextBSD: retire the radio's IO80211Controller entry, now that its
+	 * VAPs are gone and net.wlan.devices no longer lists it.
+	 */
+	ieee80211_ioreg_retire(ic);
 }
 
